.TH QUANUX-ORGANELLES 3 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Biological Sovereignty" "QuanuX System Manual"
.SH NAME
quanux-organelles \- The Ribosomes and Extension APIs for Membrane Growth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <quanux/extension_api.hpp>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QuanuX cell is genetically programmed to grow. This manual describes the API for synthesizing new organelles (connecting new external protocols, adding data adapters, or creating visual proxies) around the Strategy Nucleus.

This process is governed by the \fBCore Binding Ribosomes\fR (`execution_stack.yml`).
.SH THE CORE BINDING RIBOSOMES
When an agent or developer acts to "grow" a new membrane, they are strictly prohibited from mutating the core pin allocations. The genetic code is immutable:
.IP \[ci] 3
Core 3: The Execution Nucleus
.IP \[ci] 3
Core 5: The Sentinel Interlock
.IP \[ci] 3
Core 7: The Telemetry Ribosome
.SH GROWING THE RUSSIAN DOLL
Extensions (organelles) must be built to conform to the \fBQuanuX Native Interface\fR. 

They provide the sensory conversion of external market entropy into orderly execution logic that the Nucleus can securely digest without leaving the 64-byte `SovereignState` boundary.
